<h2 id="️-how-we-make-our-protest-signs">✂️ How We Make Our Protest Signs</h2>

<p>Here’s how you can make your own high-quality 20x30 inch protest signs, just like we do:</p>

<ol>
  <li>
    <p><strong>Designing the Layout</strong><br />
Use a program like Microsoft Publisher or any design software that supports custom canvas sizes. Set your canvas size to <strong>20 x 30 inches</strong>, and place your image how you want it.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p><strong>Printing in Sections</strong><br />
Print the image across multiple standard-size pages (usually 8.5 x 11 inches, landscape).<br />
For example, a 20x30 poster might print on 9 pages (3 across and 3 down).</p>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Cutting and Overlapping</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Cut the <strong>bottom edge</strong> of the top row pages.</li>
      <li>Leave a small <strong>white lip on the top edge</strong> of the second row so it can go underneath the top.</li>
      <li>Repeat for the third row.<br />
Do the same <strong>left to right</strong>, cutting the right edge of each page and leaving the left side to overlap.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p><strong>Assembling the Puzzle</strong><br />
Lay the pages out like a puzzle. Use clear tape (like Scotch tape) to hold the whole image together on the back.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p><strong>Mounting to Poster Board</strong><br />
Apply a thin coat of <strong>matte medium</strong> or a similar paintable adhesive to a thick poster board. Gently place your assembled printout on top, smoothing out air bubbles carefully.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p><strong>Sealing the Surface</strong><br />
Brush a thin layer of matte medium over the top. It will dry clear, giving a finished, sealed look.</p>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Backing and Reinforcement (Optional)</strong><br />
For a more durable sign, tape or glue another poster board to the back. Reinforce the edges with duct tape if desired.</li>
</ol>

<blockquote>
  <p>💡 <strong>Tip:</strong> Dollar stores often carry poster boards and tape. For matte medium, check local craft stores.</p>
</blockquote>

